          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW : D14.2(A,passive) D23.2(A,passive) D4.2(A,passive)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The Ethernet and Pi-activity LEDs will remain dark because their anodes are floating, removing intended status indication.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U10", "U11"],
      "pins": ["U10.4", "U10.5", "U11.4", "U11.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "GND1 and GND2 of both isolated CAN transceivers are tied together on the board GND net.",
      "expected": "For isolated CAN transceivers, GND1 and GND2 must be separate references to preserve galvanic isolation between the logic side and the CAN bus side, consistent with the specification's isolated CAN buses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U10.4(GND1,power_in) U10.5(GND2,power_in) U11.4(GND1,power_in) U11.5(GND2,power_in)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (`U8`, `U9`) through an isolated CAN transceiver (`U11`/companion)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The intended CAN isolation is defeated; the bus side is not galvanically isolated from logic ground, so ground-loop protection and isolation are lost.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows at least three deviations from the intended design: USB-C D- is shorted to VBUS, a 3.3V LED power net is left floating, and the isolated CAN transceivers have their separate grounds tied together."
